# trivyignore-template: v1 — ships WITH nightly.yml (its trivy job passes
# `trivyignores: .trivyignore`, and trivy treats a MISSING ignore file as a
# FATAL flag error, not an empty list — so a repo that copies the workflow
# without this file has a Trivy job that has NEVER SCANNED ANYTHING, red on
# a flag error with its real findings hidden behind it. Measured: go-enclave
# 2026-08-26, ten HIGH x/crypto CVEs sat behind the FATAL for the workflow's
# whole life — go-enclave PR #5.)
#
# Source of truth: software/templates/github-actions/.trivyignore in the
# automatethethings repo. Copy to the repo ROOT (not .github/), alongside
# copying nightly.yml. Keep it EMPTY except for CVE IDs with a dated reason:
#
#   # 2026-01-01 <who>: <why this finding does not apply here>
#   CVE-XXXX-NNNNN

# 2026-11-21: protobuf-java 2.6.1, shaded (as org.jetbrains.kotlin.protobuf)
# in lint's com.android.tools.external.com-intellij:kotlin-compiler:32.5.1
# (AGP 9.5.1); build-only, in the image's Gradle cache, not in the APK. The
# compiler reads Kotlin metadata of this build's own classpath with it, not
# untrusted input, and needs the classes, so they cannot be stripped like the
# jline ones. No lint release ships a fixed copy as of 2026-11-21 (32.5.2's
# jar is the same file). Remove with the first stable AGP whose
# kotlin-compiler drops it, or by 2026-12-21.
CVE-2021-22569 exp:2026-12-21

# 2026-11-21: protobuf-java 2.6.1, shaded (as org.jetbrains.kotlin.protobuf)
# in lint's com.android.tools.external.com-intellij:kotlin-compiler:32.5.1
# (AGP 9.5.1); build-only, in the image's Gradle cache, not in the APK. The
# compiler reads Kotlin metadata of this build's own classpath with it, not
# untrusted input, and needs the classes, so they cannot be stripped like the
# jline ones. No lint release ships a fixed copy as of 2026-11-21 (32.5.2's
# jar is the same file). Remove with the first stable AGP whose
# kotlin-compiler drops it, or by 2026-12-21.
CVE-2024-7254 exp:2026-12-21

# 2026-11-21: guava 33.4.6-jre in Gradle 9.8.1's own lib/ and guava
# 33.3.1-jre shaded (as org.jetbrains.kotlin.com.google.common) in KGP
# 2.4.21's kotlin-gradle-plugin jar; build-only, not in the APK. Every guava
# Gradle resolves, the APK's included, is pinned to 33.7.2 (catalog guavaJre,
# guavaAndroid). Gradle 9.9.2, the current stable, ships guava 33.7.2, but
# KGP 2.4.21 is still the newest stable KGP (2.5.0 is at RC) and keeps 33.3.1,
# so bumping Gradle alone does not clear the finding. Remove with the first
# stable Gradle and KGP that both ship guava 33.7.2 or later, or by 2026-12-21.
CVE-2026-102554 exp:2026-12-21
